.TH PSWorkingDirectory 3 2023-12-03 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSWorkingDirectory

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/utils.h>

.I
const char  *
.br
\fBPSWorkingDirectory\fR(\fIvoid\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns PsyC working directory, that is, by default `$HOME/.psyc`.
.br
A custom working directory can be specified at compile-time using \fIPS_WORKING_DIR\fR macro or by setting \fIPS_WORKING_DIR\fR environment variable.
.br
The function will try to automatically create the working directory if it doesn't exist.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
Path to the working directory or \fINULL\fR in case something goes wrong.

.br
\fBNOTE\fR:  it returns a static string, so it cannot be freed.
.br
